      "question": "Has Transformer 1 at site MAIN actually got worse over the past few days, or am I reacting to noise? Work out a health index and condition category for the first and the last oil sample between 2024-01-15T00:00:00.000000 and 2024-01-19T00:00:00.000000. Base each on hydrogen, methane, ethane, ethylene, acetylene, co, co2, oxygen, nitrogen, dbds, interfacial_v and dielectric_rigidity from that sample.\n\nFor each sample, give me the timestamp, the score and the category. Then give me the change in score between the two samples. Treat any change smaller than 5 points as measurement noise and call it 'stable'.\n\nIf the score dropped by 5 points or more:\n- Tell me which two or three inputs moved the most between the two samples, as a percentage change.\n- Say whether the decline is driven mainly by fault gases or mainly by oil quality.\n- Map the drivers to the single most likely failure mode from our known transformer list.\n- Run a DGA fault classification on the last sample to back that choice up, and give a confidence of high, medium or low.\n\nWhatever the result, recommend one specific next check.\n\nIf a sample is missing any of those inputs, don't estimate the missing value. Move to the next complete sample inward and tell me which timestamps you used. If only one complete sample exists in the window, give its score and category alone. In that case, say that no trend can be judged, and base the failure-mode call on the DGA classification of that sample.",
